        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is a 2-in-1 concrete stain and sealer?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              A 2-in-1 concrete stain and sealer is a single product that combines color pigment with a protective sealing resin, so one application both colors the concrete and seals it against moisture and wear. This differs from the traditional professional approach of applying an acid or water-based stain first and then a separate clear topcoat sealer in a second step.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a stain and sealer combo as good as separate stain and sealer products?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Combo products trade some performance for convenience. Separate acid stain plus a dedicated topcoat sealer produces deeper, more variegated color and generally lasts longer between maintenance coats. A quality 2-in-1 product like LastiSeal or DecoColor closes much of that gap and is significantly faster and less labor-intensive, making it the better choice for most patios, walkways, and basement floors where a subtle color refresh and protection are the goals rather than a dramatic natural-stone transformation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a concrete stain and sealer combo last?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Most acrylic stain-sealer combos last 18 months to 3 years on exterior surfaces before needing a maintenance coat, depending on traffic and sun exposure. Penetrating polymerizing products like LastiSeal can last significantly longer because the color and sealer become part of the concrete rather than sitting as a removable surface film. High-traffic areas like driveways and pool decks need more frequent recoating than shaded patios or walkways.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I use a stain and sealer combo over old sealed concrete?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Only after removing the old sealer completely. Existing sealer blocks the new product from bonding to or penetrating the concrete, causing uneven color, poor adhesion, and premature peeling. Strip old acrylic sealer with a xylene-based stripper or mechanical grinding, rinse thoroughly, and let the surface dry fully before applying a stain-sealer combo.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Which concrete stain and sealer combo has the best color?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Solvent-based combo products like DecoColor Concrete Stain and Sealer produce the deepest, most saturated color because the solvent carrier drives pigment further into the concrete's pore structure than water-based formulas. For the most authentic stone-like color depth from a permanent, non-peeling product, LastiSeal's penetrating polymerizing formula is the closest a 2-in-1 gets to a professional acid-stain look.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I use a stain and sealer combo or stain and seal separately?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Choose a 2-in-1 combo for smaller residential jobs like a patio, walkway, or basement floor where convenience, budget, and a moderate color upgrade are priorities. Choose the separate acid-stain-plus-topcoat-sealer approach for large driveways, commercial spaces, or any project where you want the maximum possible color variation and the longest-lasting professional finish, and are willing to invest in a two-step process.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

